module Text/Patterns

### The crashable thrown when pieces don't make a pattern: two captures with one name, a repetition whose range holds
### no count, an either with no alternatives, a character range that runs backward.
crashable InvalidPatternError
    ### Says what is wrong.
    message: Text

### The crashable thrown when `TextPattern.from_regex` or `BytesPattern.from_regex` is given an expression the
### patterns can't match: a backreference, lookahead or lookbehind, a shortest repetition, or a syntax error. The
### message names the position.
crashable PatternSyntaxError
    ### Says what is wrong and where.
    message: Text

### The crashable thrown when a match is asked for a capture name its pattern doesn't have.
crashable CaptureNameError
    ### The name asked for.
    name: Text

### Returns what is wrong with the pieces.
### :returns: The message.
@override
routine InvalidPatternError.crash_message() -> Text
    return me.message

### Returns what is wrong with the expression and where.
### :returns: The message.
@override
routine PatternSyntaxError.crash_message() -> Text
    return me.message

### Returns the name the pattern has no capture of.
### :returns: The message.
@override
routine CaptureNameError.crash_message() -> Text
    return f"The pattern has no capture named '{me.name}'."
